From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Casper Yang <casperyang2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:38:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Give Chromium's page dialogs a host in Brk windows

Chromium attaches passkey, HTTP sign-in, print preview, FedCM and other
tab-modal dialogs to the browser window's dialog host. Brk's window
returned no host, so constrained_window CHECKed and TabDialogManager
dereferenced null: opening such a dialog quit Brk (issue #10).

Each Brk window now owns a transparent, click-through Views widget that
becomes a child of the window while a dialog uses it (once the window is
on screen in the current Space) and registers as the browser's primary
window widget. Each page keeps one host for its life, bound to the
window that shows it, so a moved tab takes its dialog along; dialogs
centre on their page and follow window moves, resizes and page resizes.
---
